                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c6c1960c-91e9-3ba0-ac66-26971b163029",
                        "entry_id": "b382c472-340e-3e7d-997c-823b818a2db6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ., филос. термин гностицизма, означающий божественную полноту, всеобщность; совокупность небесных духовных сущностей"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "755c4b4a-6f44-44c6-9d77-60ba368f93a4",
                                "sense_id": "c6c1960c-91e9-3ba0-ac66-26971b163029",
                                "text": "Тот же (Эон), в который поместил себя Логос, совершенный в радости, был Эоном, имеющем вид вещи, будучи установленным благодаря Тому, Который явил­ся, причем это образ тех, которые существуют в Плероме, тех, которые возникли из обилия наслаждения Того, Который существует в радости."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d43c701-7327-3409-988d-d25d3dd6cb52",
                        "entry_id": "b382c472-340e-3e7d-997c-823b818a2db6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. внутренний гистоген (слой клеток) апекса корня, дифференцирующийся в клетки стелы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "46085eaa-f461-41cd-a2c4-318ca6beae02",
                        "source_entry_id": "b382c472-340e-3e7d-997c-823b818a2db6",
                        "source_sense_description": "полнота",
                        "target_lang_word": "pleroma",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pleroma",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af1de19b-6c91-3aac-b3e6-725eee5dba8a",
                                        "entry_id": "e098dc08-aee4-37d7-bab5-c151a5d19ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant of the genus Pleroma."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b9e7cff-6e5a-3488-9bae-bd04a1b924ed",
                                        "entry_id": "e098dc08-aee4-37d7-bab5-c151a5d19ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of plerome (“the central portion of the apical meristem in a growing plant root or stem which, according to the histogen theory, gives rise to the endodermis and stele”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75426d5c-25a6-463d-8da0-408657a1ef91",
                                                "sense_id": "6b9e7cff-6e5a-3488-9bae-bd04a1b924ed",
                                                "text": "In his [Jakob Eriksson's] investigations of the meristem (the tissue from which the permanent tissues are formed) by dicotyledonous roots he found four types of growth, […] In the second type only two separate meristem tissues are present in the tips of the roots; a pleroma and a common tissue, from which the primary bark and epidermis and root-cap proceed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "785901ca-14b1-4330-b701-341939cef6e5",
                                                "sense_id": "6b9e7cff-6e5a-3488-9bae-bd04a1b924ed",
                                                "text": "[I]n the pleroma of the primary meristem of roots there is not only cambium (persistent parenchyma) and procambium (forerunner of fibres and vessels), but pericambium—i.e., a special outer layer of the plerome that remains for a long time as meristem."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c201d1ca-386b-4b8b-bd6d-6a2d510033f9",
                                                "sense_id": "6b9e7cff-6e5a-3488-9bae-bd04a1b924ed",
                                                "text": "In the pleroma of hyacinth and pea roots, t#95;#123;min#125; increases along the meristem, especially in its basal part[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5f1247e-75e5-3d49-8b68-98acce7de3c5",
                                        "entry_id": "e098dc08-aee4-37d7-bab5-c151a5d19ff3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of perfect fullness, especially of God's being as incarnated in Jesus Christ."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9843b0cf-4e70-4af9-8bce-dceb0bacfac0",
                                                "sense_id": "b5f1247e-75e5-3d49-8b68-98acce7de3c5",
                                                "text": "And is all this Cabala too, and only to be uſed when People are to be gulled with noiſy Nothings? i.e. with empty Pleroma's, and ſilent Thunderclaps."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pleroma",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6dfbdce3-5e44-3ac5-b6a6-1e27e058ebc3",
                                        "entry_id": "e2e458b7-b4be-3f41-8aa1-3e7688278548",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Often preceded by the: the spiritual universe seen as the totality of the essence and powers of God."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3382add-3311-41db-b392-017688e0ae5b",
                                                "sense_id": "6dfbdce3-5e44-3ac5-b6a6-1e27e058ebc3",
                                                "text": "There is a way to comprehend the gnostic's giant onion of a world, the concentric circles, with the Pleroma beckoning there, the white heart of light, the source of that primal vision which for a second or two can recapture paradise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
